# The aspen tree PAX carries as /bin/aspen (px57; tools/mkaspen builds it).
#
# aspen is tree(1) in wolf: the maintainer's C aspen (tenseleyFlow/aspen,
# itself written with tree 2.3.2 as reference) ported (ruling #103,
# Track 14), its v1 byte-identical to tree 2.3.2 on C aspen's golden
# suite and the fixture oracle (ap00). aspen is public; its source is
# never read here beyond what building it needs (aspen's rule 1: nobody
# reads tree's source, and pax has no reason to read aspen's).
#
# aspen trunk at the time of px57 (2026-10-21): 103ba46 (ap00's merge,
# aspen#1; its src/ is ap00's gauntlet head 0db8d10's), pinned in its
# own wolf-toolchain.toml at wolf 0.2.33 / lupin 0.1.55 / wolf-std
# e036bec (staged over the archive's bundled cceda63). tools/mkaspen
# builds it with THAT toolchain, not with kernel/wolf.pin's, as
# the lope and pelt builders build theirs (px54, px15).
#
# The static binary depends on the libc.a it links (ap00): ap00's
# tools/mkaspen in an Ubuntu 24.04 container (glibc 2.39, clang 18.1.3)
# gave b34106b5bf15252e1024d1bd67839044008b5e5f4f4ae483b75821a329cda384,
# 14,497,536 bytes, twice; CI's runner 9bd08d6d7114…, 14,257,992.
ASPEN_REPO=https://github.com/wolffe-lang/aspen
ASPEN_REV=103ba4670594327acc905b9798f1ee9bde3f06c9
